        "content": "I don't actually have any physical tools, but I can help guide you through the different types of tools and functions available for your use! Here\u2019s a quick rundown:\n\n1. **Web Search Tools**:\n   - **search**: This tool helps you find information using DuckDuckGo. You provide a query, specify how many results to return (between 1 and 20), choose a language, and optionally set a region.\n     ```json\n     {\"name\": \"search\", \"arguments\": {\"query\": \"Python asyncio tutorial\", \"max_results\": 5}}\n     ```\n\n2. **Fetching Data from the Internet**:\n   - **fetch**: This function allows you to fetch data from URLs and even extract their main content as markdown, stripping out navigation elements, headers, footers, scripts, and styles.\n     ```json\n     {\"name\": \"fetch\", \"arguments\": {\"url\": \"https://example.com/page\"}}\n     ```\n\n3. **Fetching Information**:\n   - **fetch_content**: This function fetches a webpage's main text content, returning clean readable text by removing navigation elements, headers, footers, scripts, and styles.\n     ```json\n     {\"name\": \"fetch_content\", \"arguments\": {\"url\": \"https://example.com/page\"}}\n     ```\n\n4. **Dynamic Problem Solving**:\n   - **sequentialthinking**: This is a tool designed for dynamic problem-solving through thought processes that can evolve over multiple steps until reaching a satisfactory solution.\n     ```json\n     {\"name\": \"sequentialthinking\", \"arguments\": {\"thought\": \"I'm analyzing this problem step by step.\", \"nextThoughtNeeded\": true, \"total_thoughts\": 5, \"is_revision\": false}}\n     ```\n\nAll these tools are designed to help you gather information, solve problems, or even develop ideas through a structured process of analysis and reflection. Let me know if there's anything specific you'd like to try out!Sure, I'd be happy to help you use this tool. Please provide specific details about what you need assistance with or the problem